{# THE ORGANISATION RIGHT NOW — FOUR FIGURES OR NONE, like every figure row
   in the product (ruled: four to a row).

   ONE TILE PER CONTRIBUTOR. The organisation's own is how many areas there
   are; every other is a module's, at organisation scope, through the seam.
   The page lays them out, orders them and counts nothing itself.

   A SLOT NOBODY FILLED SAYS SO, and that is what makes the empty dashboard a
   report rather than a broken page: four cards reading "nothing measured" is
   an answer; four cards missing is a page somebody has to debug. #}
{% set shown = figures|slice(0, 4) %}
<div class="grid kstrip ao-kstrip" data-w="kpis">
    {% for tile in shown %}
        <div class="c kpi{{ tile.tone == 'hot' ? ' hot' : '' }}{{ tile.tone == 'bad' ? ' bad' : '' }}">
            <span class="tab">{{ tile.label }}{% if tile.live %}<span class="src">&middot; <span class="ao-live"><i></i></span></span>{% endif %}</span>
            <b class="disp">{{ tile.value }}{% if tile.unit %}<em>{{ tile.unit }}</em>{% endif %}</b>
            {% if tile.subline %}<span class="sub">{{ tile.subline }}{% if tile.alarm %} &middot; <span class="r">{{ tile.alarm }}</span>{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}
        </div>
    {% endfor %}
    {% if shown|length < 4 %}
        {% for _ in 1..(4 - shown|length) %}
            <div class="c kpi">
                <span class="tab">From the modules</span>
                <b class="disp">&mdash;</b>
                <span class="sub">nothing measured &middot; no module publishes this</span>
            </div>
        {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}
</div>
